Interoperability

bbox speaks published standards and holds no private protocol. Any
overlay host that implements BRC-22 and BRC-24 and loads the bbox host
module can carry an office and answer for it; any reader that can check
a BEEF against block headers can verify what a host answers. An envelope
can be delivered by a multicast plane (BRC-148) or submitted to each
host directly, and the records are the same either way.

